{title: 645 - God of our fathers}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]God [Cm]of [Bb7]our [Eb]fathers, Whose almightyhand
[Eb]Leads [Cm]forth in [Gm]beauty [Bb/F]all the [Fm]starry [Bb]band
[Bb]Of shining [Gb]worlds in [Fm]splendor through the [Bb]skies
[Eb/G]Our grateful songs be [Fm]fore [Gm]Thy [Bb]throne [Bb7]a [Eb]rise.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Thy [Cm]love [Bb7]divine [Ab]hath [Eb/Bb]led us [Bb]in the [Eb]past,
[Eb]In [Cm]this free [Gm]land by [Bb/F]Thee our [Fm]lot is [Bb]cast,
[Bb]Be Thou our [Gb]Ruler, [Fm]Guardian, Guide and [Bb]Stay,
[Eb/G]Thy [Ab]Word our [Eb]law, Thy [Fm]paths [Gm]our [Bb]chosen [Eb]way.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Refresh [Bb7]Thy [Eb]people on their [Bb]toilsome [Eb]way,
[Eb]Lead [Cm]us from [Gm]night to [Bb/F]never [Fm]ending [Bb]day;
[Bb]Fill all our lives [Gb]with [Fm]love and grace divine,
[Eb/G]And [Ab]glory, [Eb]laud, and [Fm]praise [Gm]be [Bb]ever [Eb]Thine.
